E245 start, size scored, group built, tag built0; 1 items ['x2']; settings {'alpha': 0.9, 'side_tols': (0.05, 0.2), 'batch': 32, 'gain_batch': 8, 'reranks': 2, 'eval_cap': 2000, 'chunk_div': 8, 'split_seed': 186001, 'reuse': ('x2', 'x10', 'moved', 'rebuilt'), 'new': ('new_few', 'new_thin'), 'sae_size': 'scored', 'sae_seed': 0, 'only': (), 'out': 'items'}; thresholds {'control_rel_tol': 0.001, 'floor_max': 1e-06, 'kl_floor': 1e-06, 'shard_hours_max': 6, 'band_min': 0.014, 'thresholds_source': "control_rel_tol: E242's revert_tol (E214's gate_tol), max |logit difference| / max |logit| between every variable stood in with gain 1 and M's own forward: a code error gives order 1, fp32 rounding of order 1e-6; the do-nothing measures this path's floor (pieces_err: every site's output rebuilt from its SAE pieces) and every item logs its own revert_err beside it, and the rehearsal (do-nothing and x10) writes both into the plan before the scored run. floor_max: E242's (E214's and E226's kl_floor): stage 0 stops if its KL floor (the larger of the do-nothing's pieces KL and revert KL) exceeds it. Not read: a tolerance whose bar tol KL(F || M) is at or under the floor, floor = the larger of the job's stage-0 floor and the item's own revert KL (E242's rule); the do-nothing reads 1 by definition. kl_floor: E226's: an item with KL(F || F_all_ablated) at or under it has no behaviour to search. shard_hours_max: the debug QoS's 2 h limit (cluster/sae_r_a.sbatch --time); stage 0 projects the job's upper bound from its measured seconds per evaluation times eval_cap times the searches. band_min: E242's (E226's) fallback when the split-half band is 0. Exact zeros, no tolerance: o_F recomputed from the module's input equals the module's output bit for bit; every gain at an unchanged site is exactly 1 and its variables stood in give KL exactly 0; all kept gives F's logits exactly; on the do-nothing every gain is exactly 1 and every variable stood in gives KL exactly 0. Amended 2026-11-21 before any scored run (sae-lead, after the rehearsal, job 62745): shard_hours_max 2 -> 6. The projection prices every search at the cap at the do-nothing's 512-window speed (0.88 s per K* and 1.23 s per stand-in evaluation, about 4.9 h per built item), so 2 h stopped every job; the copy-window items run at 0.21 s (about 56 min at the cap, inside the debug 2 h --time), and new_few and new_thin run on H100 pods, where 6 h is the gated-run limit. No rule, band or prediction changed."}
